{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1786088362898", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-ae70ddb71ebe1d2d", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "python3 -c \"\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\nimport re\n\nclass TextExtractor(HTMLParser):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.text = []\n        self.skip = False\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\n        if tag in ('script','style','nav','footer','header'):\n            self.skip = True\n        if tag in ('h1','h2','h3','h4','p','div','li','td','th','tr','table','section','figure','figcaption'):\n            self.text.append('\\n')\n    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\n        if tag in ('script','style','nav','footer','header'):\n            self.skip = False\n        if tag in ('p','div','h1','h2','h3','h4','li','td','th','tr','table','section'):\n            self.text.append('\\n')\n    def handle_data(self, data):\n        if not self.skip:\n            self.text.append(data)\n\nwith open('/tmp/affectdf_html.html','r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    html = f.read()\n\np = TextExtractor()\np.feed(html)\ntext = ''.join(p.text)\ntext = re.sub(r'\\n\\s*\\n+', '\\n\\n', text)\ntext = re.sub(r'[ \\t]+', ' ', text)\n# Find appendix sections about reproducibility\nidx = text.find('Appendix')\nif idx > 0:\n    # Search for key appendix content\n    for keyword in ['B.3', 'Reproducibility', 'Code', 'checkpoint', 'publicly available', 'github', 'License']:\n        found = text.find(keyword)\n        if found > 0:\n            print(f'--- Found \\\"{keyword}\\\" at char {found} ---')\n            print(text[max(0,found-200):found+500])\n            print()\n\" 2>&1 | head -120", "description": "Extract reproducibility info from HTML"}}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d8ef6791-7e2e-4003-9523-7588caf24412", "uuid": "0c940346-a80f-4684-a65e-708f2a0ea126"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ae70ddb71ebe1d2d", "type": "tool_result", "content": "--- Found \"B.3\" at char 21971 ---\noxtral to assess supervised LALM-based SDD. We follow the original training configurations for all trainable baselines. Additional model and reproducibility details are provided in Appendices B.2 and B.3. LALM inference and fine-tuning details are provided in Appendices C.2 and D.\n\n5 Results\n\n5.1 Emotion Breaks Cross-Domain Generalization\n\nTable 3: Emotion-wise EER (%) results. Neutral (N), Happy (H), Angry (A), Sad (S), Surprise (Su).\n\nModel\n\nTrain Data\n\nEmoFake\n\nAffectDF\n\nN\n\nH\n\nA\n\nS\n\nSu\n\nN\n\nH\n\nA\n\nS\n\nSu\n\nRawNet2\n\nASVspoof2019\n\n19.66\n\n16.57\n\n23.00\n\n–\n\n28.54\n\n56.21\n\n60.93\n\n63.82\n\n48.88\n\n64.28\n\nAASIST\n\nASVspoof2019\n\n17.20\n\n11.63\n\n15.00\n\n–\n\n13.57\n\n65.45\n\n61.07\n\n50.91\n\n41.82\n\n48.56\n\nXLSR-SLS\n\nAS\n\n--- Found \"Reproducibility\" at char 78668 ---\nLL-based inference strategy, with further details provided in Appendix D. Table 11 summarizes these settings.\n\nTable 11: \nAudio preprocessing, training, and inference details for SDD systems.\n\nModel\n\nReproducibility Details\n\nRawNet2\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples (∼\\sim4 s).\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; best checkpoint selected based on the lowest development loss.\n\nAASIST\n\nAudio: Converted to mono, resampled to 16 kHz, and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples.\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10\n\n--- Found \"checkpoint\" at char 69989 ---\nrceiver encoder, and generates target acoustic tokens with a GPT-style autoregressive decoder, which are then converted to waveform using a HiFiGAN vocoder. In our experiments, we use the GenVC-Large checkpoint, which is initialized from GenVC-Small and further trained with additional English speech from CommonVoice-EN and MLS-EN.\n\nConsistencyVC.\n\nGuo et al. (2023) ConsistencyVC is a VITS-style voice conversion model that combines a content encoder, a jointly trained speaker encoder, a flow module, a posterior encoder, and a HiFi-GAN-based decoder. The model uses PPG features for expressive voice conversion, while the speaker encoder extracts reference-speaker information from the mel-spectr\n\n--- Found \"publicly available\" at char 8557 ---\nest of our knowledge, AffectDF is the first benchmark for systematically evaluating speech deepfake detection under diverse emotionally expressive spoofing attacks. AffectDF and related resources are publicly available.111AffectDF: https://affectdf33-data.github.io/AffectDF-Data/\n\n2 Related Work", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d8ef6791-7e2e-4003-9523-7588caf24412", "uuid": "0084e2dc-5ba1-48d4-b3c6-cc09ab97e151", "timestamp": "2026-08-07T07:39:57.832Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "--- Found \"B.3\" at char 21971 ---\noxtral to assess supervised LALM-based SDD. We follow the original training configurations for all trainable baselines. Additional model and reproducibility details are provided in Appendices B.2 and B.3. LALM inference and fine-tuning details are provided in Appendices C.2 and D.\n\n5 Results\n\n5.1 Emotion Breaks Cross-Domain Generalization\n\nTable 3: Emotion-wise EER (%) results. Neutral (N), Happy (H), Angry (A), Sad (S), Surprise (Su).\n\nModel\n\nTrain Data\n\nEmoFake\n\nAffectDF\n\nN\n\nH\n\nA\n\nS\n\nSu\n\nN\n\nH\n\nA\n\nS\n\nSu\n\nRawNet2\n\nASVspoof2019\n\n19.66\n\n16.57\n\n23.00\n\n–\n\n28.54\n\n56.21\n\n60.93\n\n63.82\n\n48.88\n\n64.28\n\nAASIST\n\nASVspoof2019\n\n17.20\n\n11.63\n\n15.00\n\n–\n\n13.57\n\n65.45\n\n61.07\n\n50.91\n\n41.82\n\n48.56\n\nXLSR-SLS\n\nAS\n\n--- Found \"Reproducibility\" at char 78668 ---\nLL-based inference strategy, with further details provided in Appendix D. Table 11 summarizes these settings.\n\nTable 11: \nAudio preprocessing, training, and inference details for SDD systems.\n\nModel\n\nReproducibility Details\n\nRawNet2\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples (∼\\sim4 s).\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; best checkpoint selected based on the lowest development loss.\n\nAASIST\n\nAudio: Converted to mono, resampled to 16 kHz, and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples.\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10\n\n--- Found \"checkpoint\" at char 69989 ---\nrceiver encoder, and generates target acoustic tokens with a GPT-style autoregressive decoder, which are then converted to waveform using a HiFiGAN vocoder. In our experiments, we use the GenVC-Large checkpoint, which is initialized from GenVC-Small and further trained with additional English speech from CommonVoice-EN and MLS-EN.\n\nConsistencyVC.\n\nGuo et al. (2023) ConsistencyVC is a VITS-style voice conversion model that combines a content encoder, a jointly trained speaker encoder, a flow module, a posterior encoder, and a HiFi-GAN-based decoder. The model uses PPG features for expressive voice conversion, while the speaker encoder extracts reference-speaker information from the mel-spectr\n\n--- Found \"publicly available\" at char 8557 ---\nest of our knowledge, AffectDF is the first benchmark for systematically evaluating speech deepfake detection under diverse emotionally expressive spoofing attacks. AffectDF and related resources are publicly available.111AffectDF: https://affectdf33-data.github.io/AffectDF-Data/\n\n2 Related Work", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
