{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-937ef6ac0cd77ade", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Reproducibility Details\n\nRawNet2\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples (∼\\sim4 s).\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; best checkpoint selected based on the lowest development loss.\n\nAASIST\n\nAudio: Converted to mono, resampled to 16 kHz, and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples.\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; best checkpoint selected based on the lowest development loss.\n\nXLSR-SLS\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples (∼\\sim4 s). RawBoost augmentation is used during training.\nTraining: Up to 50 epochs; batch size 5; learning rate 1×10−61\\times 10^{-6}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy.\n\nXLSR-Mamba\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 66,800 samples (∼\\sim4.2 s). RawBoost augmentation is used during training.\nTraining: 7 epochs; batch size 20; learning rate 1×10−61\\times 10^{-6}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; final-epoch checkpoint used for evaluation.\n\nProSDD\n\nAudio: Converted to mono, resampled to 16 kHz, and padded/cropped to 64,000 samples (4 s). RawBoost is applied to 50% of samples during Stage-II training.\nTraining: Initialized from the released Stage-I checkpoint and trained for Stage II for 50 epochs; batch size 64; learning rates 1×10−61\\times 10^{-6}, 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}, and 1×10−51\\times 10^{-5} for the XLS-R backbone, projection layer, and classifier, respectively; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy and supervised masked-prediction losses. Speaker and prosodic embeddings are extracted using the released code.\n\nQwen-2.5-Omni\n\nThe input audio is passed to the model processor. At inference, the model is prompted to generate a single score in [0,1][0,1], interpreted as the probability of fake, where 0 denotes real and 1 denotes fake. A maximum of 6 generated tokens is used, and three inference runs are conducted.\n\nQwen-3.0-Omni\n\nThe input audio is passed to the model processor. At inference, the model is prompted to generate a single score in [0,1][0,1], interpreted as the probability of fake, where 0 denotes real and 1 denotes fake. Sampled decoding is used with temperature 0.7, top-p=0.9p=0.9, and a maximum of 6 generated tokens; three inference runs are conducted.\n\nVoxtral\n\nAudio: Loaded as mono 24 kHz audio and passed through the model’s audio encoder.\nInference: The model is prompted to generate a single score in [0,1][0,1], interpreted as the probability of fake, where 0 denotes real and 1 denotes fake. Sampled decoding is used with temperature 0.2, top-p=0.95p=0.95, and a maximum of 10 generated tokens; three inference runs are conducted.\n\nVoxtral-FT\n\nAudio: Loaded as mono 24 kHz audio and passed through the model’s audio encoder.\nTraining: Supervised LoRA", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d8ef6791-7e2e-4003-9523-7588caf24412", "uuid": "55246f89-6bf9-4dce-81c3-30ed08f52812", "timestamp": "2026-08-07T07:40:30.183Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "Reproducibility Details\n\nRawNet2\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples (∼\\sim4 s).\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; best checkpoint selected based on the lowest development loss.\n\nAASIST\n\nAudio: Converted to mono, resampled to 16 kHz, and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples.\nTraining: 50 epochs; batch size 32; Adam optimizer; learning rate 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; best checkpoint selected based on the lowest development loss.\n\nXLSR-SLS\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 64,600 samples (∼\\sim4 s). RawBoost augmentation is used during training.\nTraining: Up to 50 epochs; batch size 5; learning rate 1×10−61\\times 10^{-6}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy.\n\nXLSR-Mamba\n\nAudio: Loaded as 16 kHz mono and padded/cropped to 66,800 samples (∼\\sim4.2 s). RawBoost augmentation is used during training.\nTraining: 7 epochs; batch size 20; learning rate 1×10−61\\times 10^{-6}; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy; final-epoch checkpoint used for evaluation.\n\nProSDD\n\nAudio: Converted to mono, resampled to 16 kHz, and padded/cropped to 64,000 samples (4 s). RawBoost is applied to 50% of samples during Stage-II training.\nTraining: Initialized from the released Stage-I checkpoint and trained for Stage II for 50 epochs; batch size 64; learning rates 1×10−61\\times 10^{-6}, 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}, and 1×10−51\\times 10^{-5} for the XLS-R backbone, projection layer, and classifier, respectively; weight decay 1×10−41\\times 10^{-4}; weighted cross-entropy and supervised masked-prediction losses. Speaker and prosodic embeddings are extracted using the released code.\n\nQwen-2.5-Omni\n\nThe input audio is passed to the model processor. At inference, the model is prompted to generate a single score in [0,1][0,1], interpreted as the probability of fake, where 0 denotes real and 1 denotes fake. A maximum of 6 generated tokens is used, and three inference runs are conducted.\n\nQwen-3.0-Omni\n\nThe input audio is passed to the model processor. At inference, the model is prompted to generate a single score in [0,1][0,1], interpreted as the probability of fake, where 0 denotes real and 1 denotes fake. Sampled decoding is used with temperature 0.7, top-p=0.9p=0.9, and a maximum of 6 generated tokens; three inference runs are conducted.\n\nVoxtral\n\nAudio: Loaded as mono 24 kHz audio and passed through the model’s audio encoder.\nInference: The model is prompted to generate a single score in [0,1][0,1], interpreted as the probability of fake, where 0 denotes real and 1 denotes fake. Sampled decoding is used with temperature 0.2, top-p=0.95p=0.95, and a maximum of 10 generated tokens; three inference runs are conducted.\n\nVoxtral-FT\n\nAudio: Loaded as mono 24 kHz audio and passed through the model’s audio encoder.\nTraining: Supervised LoRA", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
